              "question": "<p>Normally, the natural flora on the skin and GIT contains bacteria that release toxins which keep the fungi in check, and fungi that release toxins which keep the bacteria in check. Candida albicans infection (candidiasis), which is a fungal infection of the mouth, GIT and or vagina can occur due to antibiotic use because the antibiotics kill off many of the protective bacteria within the bacterial flora.&nbsp;</p>\n"
